From 6150630285ff55f0b0bba877cce52106df757236 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:03:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [TSReader] Drop the rest of a copied frame after a seek

A seek can return a copy of a frame whose PES starts before the position
where the read after the seek starts. The rest of that frame can follow
after that position in a PES of its own, as the picture PES of a key
frame whose parameter sets came in a PES before the segment end. The
read after the seek parsed that PES again, and returned the key frame a
second time without its parameter sets.

ElementaryStream::NextFramePosition() gives the stream position of the
PES where the next frame starts, and ContinueAfterCopy() replaces
ContinueDecode(): after the next reset, the stream drops the PES that
start before that position. If the end of the data completed the copied
frame, the stream drops the data up to the next PES with a PTS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
